Write sliderFill through the appearance writer

sliderFill holds an appearance, and the writer sends it through
CFG_WRITE_ENTRY. That macro calls the one-argument toStr, whose only
match for an enumeration is the boolean form. Every value of the combo
box therefore reaches the file as the word true. The reader asks
toAppearance for that word and finds no appearance of that name. The
read takes the default, so the chosen groove fill never survives one
save.

Send the field through CFG_WRITE_APPEARANCE_ENTRY with APP_ALLOW_BASIC,
the range that the reader already asks for. The other 23 appearance
fields already use an appearance writer. An older file that holds the
word true still reads as the default, because toAppearance answers no
appearance for it.

The change sits on the branch work/config-io of the local tree, as commit 14 of 18.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/common/config_file.cpp b/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
index 8f1b5e29..855c4136 100644
--- a/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
+++ b/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
@@ -2436,7 +2436,7 @@ bool qtcWriteConfig(KConfig *cfg, const Options &opts, const Options &def, bool
         CFG_WRITE_APPEARANCE_ENTRY(sunkenAppearance, APP_ALLOW_BASIC);
         CFG_WRITE_APPEARANCE_ENTRY(sbarBgndAppearance, APP_ALLOW_BASIC);
         CFG_WRITE_APPEARANCE_ENTRY(tooltipAppearance, APP_ALLOW_BASIC);
-        CFG_WRITE_ENTRY(sliderFill);
+        CFG_WRITE_APPEARANCE_ENTRY(sliderFill, APP_ALLOW_BASIC);
         CFG_WRITE_ENTRY(progressGrooveColor);
         CFG_WRITE_ENTRY(focus);
         CFG_WRITE_ENTRY(lvButton);
